theorem value-at-one
  note        Cited below with its f filled by a define the build holds as k, the letter this binds.
  let f : ℕ → ℝ                                                       (H1)
  assume for all k ∈ ℕ, f(k) = k + 1                                  (H2)
  then f(1) = 1 + 1

1.  f(1) = 1 + 1
    instantiate k := 1 in H2

theorem a-define-filling-a-cited-function
  note        The cited theorem's bound k is moved apart from the define's letter. t's type is said once: its rule j + 1 is a number for every j ∈ ℕ.
  let t(j) = j + 1, for j ∈ ℕ                                         (D1)
         reads one more
  then t(1) = 1 + 1

1.  For all j ∈ ℕ, t(j) = j + 1.
    D1

2.  t(1) = 1 + 1
    thm:value-at-one f := t, from 1
